    given-names: Dong Hyun
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9883-0229"
    affiliation: "Inha University College of Medicine"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Raspberry-Kim/donghyun-lab4"
url: "https://raspberry-kim.github.io/donghyun-lab4/"
abstract: >-
  Donghyunjeon is a browser-based, noncommercial turn-based strategy
  simulation laboratory for one player against a computer opponent (normal
  difficulty, no fog of war). The map, commanders, first move and starting
  funds are chosen only through programs written in the esoteric programming
  language Donghyun-lang; the battle itself is played with the keyboard
  (arrow keys, X confirm, Z cancel, S next unit, A info) or on-screen buttons.
  It includes 20 original maps built with two-fold rotational symmetry,
  five original commanders, a heuristic computer opponent, and saving and
  loading in browser slots or as files. It is a fan-inspired hobby work in
  the genre of grid tactics games; it is not affiliated with or endorsed by
  Nintendo or Intelligent Systems, and it contains none of their sprites,
  names, maps or music. All art, names and maps are original. The MIT license
  applies to the application code, documentation and artwork; the fonts are
  under the SIL Open Font License. See LICENSE and CREDITS.md.
keywords:
  - turn-based strategy
  - tactics game
  - game AI
  - pixel art
  - esoteric programming language
  - JavaScript
